    "title": "From Ruins to Skyscrapers",
    "subtitle": "How a poor land grew into a strong country.",
    "body": "Long ago, Korea was very poor. A big war broke the country. Many homes and roads lay in <u>ruins</u>. People had little food or money.\n\nBut they did not give up. They worked hard to build a new country. Workers built many factories. The factories made shoes, cloth, and ships.\n\nKorea sold these goods to other lands. This selling is called export. The money came back and helped the country grow. Soon people <mark>built new roads and tall buildings</mark>.\n\nThis fast growth is called the Miracle on the Han River. Later, Korea made cars, phones, and computers. Today, tall skyscrapers fill the cities. A poor land grew into a strong country.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/17.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "On the left, war ruins; on the right, a city of bright skyscrapers."
  },
